<h2>Start watching</h2>
<p>Choose a Lichess TV channel, an arena or a tournament from the home screen. For tournaments, choose a round and then a board. Coverage and timing depend on the Lichess relay.</p>
<h2>Alerts stopped arriving</h2>
<p>On iPhone or iPad, open Settings → Notifications in Chess TV. Check permission, mute and quiet hours, then try Reset push notifications. This repairs registration and restores your follows. If iOS has disabled notifications, enable them in iOS Settings first. Push delivery can be delayed by the system and needs a physical device.</p>
<h2>Apple Watch</h2>
<p>Open Chess TV on the paired iPhone to sync your follows. A saved board may remain visible while the Watch is disconnected. Open the Watch app in the foreground to refresh it.</p>
<h2>Apple Music on TV</h2>
<p>Connect Apple Music from Settings on Apple TV. Playback requires an eligible Apple Music subscription and authorization. Chess viewing does not require Music access.</p>
